        "file_upload": false,
        "spell_check": false,
        "word_limit_enabled": false
      },
      "item_body": "<p>Simplify (a + b) x (a - b) using only the algebraic properties of the cross product. Do not use components. State each property you use by name. Then, assuming |a| = |b|, show that (a + b) dot (a - b) = 0 and explain in full sentences what this means geometrically for the parallelogram with sides a and b.</p>",
